{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/467615-white-wolf-and-vampire-the-masquerade-mentioned-briefly-in-vice-article","id":467615,"title":"White Wolf and Vampire the Masquerade mentioned, briefly, in Vice article","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-03T11:02:40-07:00","id":467615,"title":"White Wolf and Vampire the Masquerade mentioned, briefly, in Vice article","content":"I suppose the topic title says it all.<br /> <br /> Here's the article.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.vice.com/read/fuck-for-satan-the-new-wave-of-sex-centric-rpgs-456\" target=\"_blank\">'Fuck for Satan': The New Generation of Sex-Centric Tabletop RPGs</a><br /> <br /> Don't get too offended just by the title, it's referring to an adventure in Lamentations of the Flame Princess. White Wolf is only mentioned in one paragraph, which you can see here if you don't want to check out the full article.<br /> <br /> 'It wasn't until the late 80s and early 90s that companies like White Wolf started to release sex-tinged games like 1991's Vampire: The Masquerade, which centered around lovelorn goth-punk vampires. Though arguably making romance and eroticism important components of the game was a step forward, today The Masquerade seems outdated when viewed through the lens of today's sex-positive, LGBT-inclusive, and feminist values\u2014as do most RPGs from earlier eras. After all, tabletop games reflect the fantasies of their makers and players, and fantasies can easily become colored by biases and misconceptions.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-03-2015, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T01:18:57-07:00","id":469246,"title":"","content":"They miss out that VtM and other White Wolf games had a lot of LGBT, sex-positive and feminist themes in their games and was, in fact, a major forerunner for inclusiveness in RPGs. Though common now, at the time White Wolf was definitely ahead of the pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T03:49:20-07:00","id":469278,"title":"","content":"The article starts off talking about advances in inclusivity and then focuses on games that in one case is just fucking awful and the other has a couple of disturbing pieces of artwork. WTF did I just read? What was the point of the article? Vice usually has better written articles, this left me confused as to its point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T04:48:36-07:00","id":469286,"title":"","content":"They've really broadened who posts there and a lot of them are semi-advertisements, like this one seemed to be for Lament of the Flame Princess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T18:15:55-07:00","id":469713,"title":"","content":"Somehow related, the article reminded me of a conversation I had with some of my players on the philosophical changes from old WW to new OP.<br /> <br /> I think White Wolf games lost a lot of its appeal to young people looking for a hobby to express themselves after its games dropped their edginess. Sure, it retained a lot of older players that were now maturing. But while the earlier versions of cWoD (just like the original Hellblazer series which I am very fond of) were wealthier in &quot;edge&quot; and social critique, the new games at best maintain a superficial message of inclusion.<br /> <br /> We're past that, only a few bad apples would oppose inclusion. It's no longer provocative (as in thought-provocative) to include a homosexual or empowered female character in a book here and there. Punk needs to make a comeback (as in Punk Gothic), although I do not mean it in the literal sense of adding more elements from the Punk subculture to the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Cops are shooting African Americans, Southern Europe is bleeding with poverty, homelessness and high suicide rates. Governments and big corporations openly admit they are spying on us. Inequality is at an <b>all-time high</b>. I repeat, <b>all-time high</b>. The anarchocapitalists tell us that's okay, that inequality leads to equality just like suicide cures cancer. Had technology not advanced so much in the 20th century, we would not be able to feed a huge percentage of the total population.<br /> <br /> NWoD, as written, is milder than the real world for example.<br /> <br /> Of course, being from Greece, my viewpoint is biased. But aren't they all? You've got your neat little organizations, always plotting and researching, preparing for a conflict that never comes. &quot;Lest we step on anyone's toes&quot; seems to be the zeitgeist of our time. Well fuck it. Anyone who knows anyone in Greece has witnessed a suicide attempt for financial reasons. I'm not saying RPGs should pick a side on issues that might alienate some group of players. But the world is getting shittier by the day, quantitatively and qualitatively. I study Politics and never have I seen so much pessimism in a department full of young people that started out wanting to contribute to society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T19:18:03-07:00","id":469773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/467615-white-wolf-and-vampire-the-masquerade-mentioned-briefly-in-vice-article?p=469713#post469713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NWoD, as written, is milder than the real world for example.<br /> <br /> Of course, being from Greece, my viewpoint is biased. But aren't they all? You've got your neat little organizations, always plotting and researching, preparing for a conflict that never comes. &quot;Lest we step on anyone's toes&quot; seems to be the zeitgeist of our time. Well fuck it. Anyone who knows anyone in Greece has witnessed a suicide attempt for financial reasons. I'm not saying RPGs should pick a side on issues that might alienate some group of players. But the world is getting shittier by the day, quantitatively and qualitatively. I study Politics and never have I seen so much pessimism in a department full of young people that started out wanting to contribute to society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on where in the world you are.<br /> <br /> North america has an increasing grid on the poor system set up. There's the whole disproportionate percentage of the population in prison thing. There's the increasing jail time for any crime, to the point where your only hope of getting out in a sane time ts to volunteer for one of the &quot;work training&quot; systems where you work for the company that owns the prison under the guise of rehabilitation. There's the fun detail that If you commit a minor civil offense you are required to pay a fine, if you can't pay the fine immediately (typically because you have limited income) you are handed over to a corporation who will charge you for the advantage of paying it off bit by bit... that in reality endlessly increases the amount owed. And that's besides the government monitoring, highly questionable practices in the name of security such as gitmo or extraordinary rendition. So yes, things are getting worse and worse.<br /> <br /> And that's *before* you add in the increasing issues from mechanization and automation. the &quot;Western World&quot; is going to be facing a disaster of a situation in a decade with large amounts of the workforce being obsoleted.<br /> <br /> <br /> That having been said, safety is still on the rise. You are far less likely to be the victim of a violent crime now that in even the 70's. Accepting of course that police excesses are not considered crimes.<br /> <br /> The quality of life in South America, Central America, Africa, China, India Pakistan and a host of other generally considered poor/desperate places have been significantly improving however. China is going gangbusters for instance, generating a large number of very rich people and a steadily increasing and broad middle class.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T21:41:40-07:00","id":469860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/467615-white-wolf-and-vampire-the-masquerade-mentioned-briefly-in-vice-article?p=469773#post469773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on where in the world you are.<br /> <br /> North america has an increasing grid on the poor system set up. There's the whole disproportionate percentage of the population in prison thing. There's the increasing jail time for any crime, to the point where your only hope of getting out in a sane time ts to volunteer for one of the &quot;work training&quot; systems where you work for the company that owns the prison under the guise of rehabilitation. There's the fun detail that If you commit a minor civil offense you are required to pay a fine, if you can't pay the fine immediately (typically because you have limited income) you are handed over to a corporation who will charge you for the advantage of paying it off bit by bit... that in reality endlessly increases the amount owed. And that's besides the government monitoring, highly questionable practices in the name of security such as gitmo or extraordinary rendition. So yes, things are getting worse and worse.<br /> <br /> And that's *before* you add in the increasing issues from mechanization and automation. the &quot;Western World&quot; is going to be facing a disaster of a situation in a decade with large amounts of the workforce being obsoleted.<br /> <br /> <br /> That having been said, safety is still on the rise. You are far less likely to be the victim of a violent crime now that in even the 70's. Accepting of course that police excesses are not considered crimes.<br /> <br /> The quality of life in South America, Central America, Africa, China, India Pakistan and a host of other generally considered poor/desperate places have been significantly improving however. China is going gangbusters for instance, generating a large number of very rich people and a steadily increasing and broad middle class.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Definitely, I agree 100%. What I (poorly) tried to say was that back in middleschool, WW settings made sense, felt real, plausible and scary. Technocracy vs the Order of Hermes, that was based on the very real philosophical battle between materialists and metaphysicists. Growing up in Greece, we felt that dualism, that Cold War zeitgeist, and the influence of Vampire elders (Requiem was our first game but it was still early enough that VtM was used to fill in the blanks) resonated with our sense of wonder about adult life. Greek society was still torn along the lines of Communism vs. Nationalism, and the rich appeared invisible and untouchable. It was the time of Satanism scare in Greece, and I recall an incident with some students getting expelled for a couple of days for reading an anti-Christian publication named &quot;The Bible of Nod&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The new focus on the strictly personal/local detective of the unknown stories, while great, can only generate so much appeal and explore only so many philosophical concepts. A third World of Darkness should go back to those roots, of capturing the issues facing our society, the ones we are not comfortable discussing or picking sides on. Something which videogames have been doing quite successfully as of late, such as Bioshock Infinite.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying this is my cup of tea, like the rest of the community I grew up as well. But a teenager or young adult growing up, groomed to join an ever-increasing army of the unemployed, is not the least bit interested to play an amnesiac elder vampire and roleplay his drama and shock. Hell, if it weren't for White Wolf, half of us would not get into metal and gothic music, would not have met our long-time girlfriends (and now wives) and would not have immersed knee-deep in counter-culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T11:18:58-07:00","id":470278,"title":"","content":"I remember reading some parts of the new Book of the Wyrm and thinking that some aspects of Pentex are just sort of small time compared to real life corporations. Obviously the worship of alien beings is out, but in their inhumanity to get better profits it's pretty surprising what lengths they will go to, providing you're not a pessimist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T02:56:35-07:00","id":476814,"title":"","content":"I graduated with a business degree. College was like a Pentex board meeting (back stabbing, throat cutting behavior), real corporate environments were so much worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T07:23:47-07:00","id":476932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/467615-white-wolf-and-vampire-the-masquerade-mentioned-briefly-in-vice-article?p=476814#post476814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I graduated with a business degree. College was like a Pentex board meeting (back stabbing, throat cutting behavior), real corporate environments were so much worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I attended business school at a US institution and maintained a GPA of above 3.8/4 throughout my first two years there. Dropped out because of the mentality of students and then attended a UK institution (started from scratch) focusing on a double major (Business and Politics). Business was just as bad, so I switched to Politics.<br /> <br /> I began focusing on Marxism, as a reaction. Politics was no better, filled with helpless, ageing academics that feared losing funding for their papers and seminars too much to speak out against any issue of importance that might've upset the &quot;powers that be&quot;. Then I looked around Communist parties and saw just as many hierarchies and Machiavellian politics, so that now I became a direct democrat (or &quot;laocrat&quot; as I prefer to call it, to differentiate from represenativism). I think the fault lies in structures, specifically the all mighty pyramid. Any group or organisation that's got a top-down, pyramid structure, coupled with a lack of punishing openness and accountability, is bound to lead to corruption at the VERY LEAST.<br /> <br /> That's my response to some nWoD players I get who complain that whenever I actively include elder vampires in my Requiem chronicles, I make them power-hungry control freaks. Anything less and we are playing in a world that is <b>actually</b> an improvement over our own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T18:33:00-07:00","id":477427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=